rding Tailoring and Garment Cutting Certificate Course, Organized by Assamese & Sansk\n2026-03-13\nView File\nChatra Divas, Celebration of Birth Anniversary of Bodofa Upendra Nath Brahma\nCelebration of the Birth Centenary of Dr. Bhupen Hazarika, 08-09-2025\nOne Day Workshop on Performance of Bihu and Folk Instruments, organised by Departments of English, A\nParents meeting, Assamese, Economics, History &amp; Sanskrit, 28-02-2026\nEducational Tour Report, Assamese Department, 08-02-2026\nProfile\nFaculty Members\nActivities\nAchievements\nQuestion Paper\nSyllabus\nPO & CO\nNewsletter\nProfile\nThe Department of Assamese has been a foundational pillar of the institution since its establishment in 1993. It was initiated with a vision to promote the rich linguistic and literary heritage of Assam and to cultivate a deep sense of cultural identity among students. Over the years, the department has evolved into a vibrant centre of learning, offering both Major and Minor programmes with consistent academic success. The department is committed to preserving and disseminating Assamese literature while simultaneously engaging with contemporary literary theories and interdisciplinary approaches. It plays a significant role in promoting regional knowledge systems in alignment with the principles of NEP 2020. The curriculum is designed to integrate traditional literary studies with modern critical perspectives, ensuring holistic intellectual development. The department encourages research-oriented learning and critical inquiry among students. It also focuses on developing language proficiency, analytical skills, and creative expression. Faculty members actively mentor students to participate in academic and cultural activities. Through seminars, field studies, and project-based learning, the department fosters experiential and participatory education. It continues to contribute to the academic and cultural landscape of the institution with dedication and excellence.\nFaculty Mem